Explicit breaking would add a local bias, $H_{\rm explicit}
  =-J\sum_{\langle ij\rangle}s_i s_j-h\sum_i s_i,
  \qquad h\ne0.$ Then heads and tails do not have equal energy even at one isolated site, and there is only one preferred vacuum. In spontaneous breaking $h=0$: the local rules are symmetric and the two vacua remain degenerate, but the system occupies one of them.

