p.src:
The weakness of beta decay is then traced not to an exceptionally tiny $g_w$, but to the heavy mediator. In distance space, mass cuts off the propagator beyond the Compton scale $\hbar/(m_Wc)$. In momentum space, $\mathcal A_{\rm weak}
  \sim\frac{g_w^2}{k^2+m_W^2}
  \simeq\frac{g_w^2}{m_W^2}$ at nuclear momenta. Old low-energy experiments measured this combination as the Fermi constant.

